{
  "_": "The font catalogue — the ONE list of faces Recto knows. The build writes it, with which files are present, to generated/fonts.json; text_tool builds the toolbar's font menu and the @font-face rules from that, and resolves (family, bold, italic) to a file for HarfBuzz widths. Files live beside this file (web/assets/fonts/); `python3 tools/dev/fonts_setup.py` builds them: the URW faces are converted from tol0's certified CFFs, the Windows faces copied from C:/Windows/Fonts. Family names are exactly what tol0's set-fonts table uses, so an OCR line names its face in the same words.",
